---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Barcode Product Database Coverage | BarcodeNest" description="Explore BarcodeNest coverage across 4.35M+ food, beauty, pet food and general products, with transparent source attribution and coverage limits." current="data">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About the data</div><h1>One barcode index across multiple product categories.</h1><p class="lede">BarcodeNest validates identifiers, indexes product records, normalises selected fields, and exposes consistent API responses—with provenance kept visible.</p></div></header>

  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="content-grid">
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Indexed, not proxied</h3><p>Customer barcode lookups query BarcodeNest’s own indexed database. They do not call upstream data providers live during each request.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Canonical identifiers</h3><p>Accepted barcodes are validated and mapped to a zero-padded GTIN-14 identity to help equivalent representations resolve consistently.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Structured responses</h3><p>Product identity, product attributes, and source metadata are separated into a predictable response schema.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Visible provenance</h3><p>Contributing sources remain separately recorded. BarcodeNest does not claim ownership of third-party product data.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container metric-row"><div class="big-metric">4.35M<span>+</span></div><div><div class="eyebrow">Current coverage</div><h2>A multi-source product index.</h2><p class="lede">The production database contains more than 4.35 million canonical products. Coverage is global, with especially strong grocery depth in Europe and growing US and non-food coverage.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="eyebrow">What is covered</div><h2>A practical cross-section of packaged products.</h2><p class="lede">These are broad coverage categories, not guarantees that every product or barcode in each category is present.</p></div><div class="content-grid">
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Food &amp; beverages</h3><p>Packaged groceries, beverages, branded foods, ingredients, snacks, pantry products, and nutrition-related products.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Beauty &amp; personal care</h3><p>Cosmetics, skincare, haircare, fragrances, hygiene products, and related personal-care items.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Pet food</h3><p>Packaged pet foods, treats, and nutrition products for dogs, cats, and other companion animals.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>General packaged products</h3><p>A growing long tail of household and retail products outside food, beauty, and pet-food categories.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><div class="eyebrow">Data sources</div><h2>Transparent attribution and reuse.</h2><p>BarcodeNest combines product information from <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/" rel="external"><u>Open Food Facts</u></a>, <a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/" rel="external"><u>USDA FoodData Central</u></a>, <a href="https://world.openbeautyfacts.org/" rel="external"><u>Open Beauty Facts</u></a>, <a href="https://world.openpetfoodfacts.org/" rel="external"><u>Open Pet Food Facts</u></a>, and <a href="https://world.openproductsfacts.org/" rel="external"><u>Open Products Facts</u></a>. BarcodeNest provides an indexed, normalised API layer and does not claim ownership of third-party data or imply endorsement by its sources.</p><p>The Open Facts databases are made available under the <a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/" rel="external"><u>Open Database License (ODbL)</u></a>. USDA FoodData Central data is public domain and published under CC0. Individual database contents and images can have separate licensing considerations; review each source’s current terms for your particular reuse.</p><div class="callout">Every contributing source remains separately recorded internally, even when several sources resolve to the same canonical GTIN.</div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><div class="eyebrow">Coverage limits</div><h2>What to expect.</h2><p class="lede">Coverage is not universal. Field completeness varies by product, source, market, and geography. Names and brands are more common than ingredients, allergens, nutrition, or images, and data can be incomplete or out of date.</p><p>Evaluate the API with barcodes representative of your users, regions, and categories. For questions about a particular use case, email <a href="mailto:support@barcodenest.com"><u>support@barcodenest.com</u></a>.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
